WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.637
Three areas carry most
of the planning weight.

2
00:00:02.637 --> 00:00:04.038
Topology first.

3
00:00:04.038 --> 00:00:07.300
Active Directory has five
operations master roles.

4
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:11.950
Two are forest-wide, the schema
master and the domain naming master.

5
00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:15.335
Three exist in every
domain: the PDC emulator,

6
00:00:15.335 --> 00:00:18.812
the RID master and the
infrastructure master.

7
00:00:18.812 --> 00:00:23.512
So a three-domain forest has eleven
role holders to record, not five.

8
00:00:23.512 --> 00:00:26.239
The PDC emulator in
the forest root is also

9
00:00:26.239 --> 00:00:29.200
the authoritative time
source for the forest.

10
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.037
Record every functional level
and flag two conditions.

11
00:00:33.037 --> 00:00:38.806
A level below Windows Server 2016
blocks the domain controller refresh,

12
00:00:38.806 --> 00:00:44.575
because a Server 2025 controller can
join only a domain at 2016 or higher.

13
00:00:44.575 --> 00:00:46.225
And mixed domain levels.

14
00:00:46.225 --> 00:00:51.625
Server 2025 is the first new
functional level since 2016.

15
00:00:51.625 --> 00:00:55.505
Capture site links with cost and
interval, and the subnet map:

16
00:00:55.505 --> 00:00:59.850
an unmapped subnet sends clients
to arbitrary domain controllers.

17
00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:02.025
Second, the OU hierarchy.

18
00:01:02.025 --> 00:01:05.259
The goal is to capture what
the tree encodes so the

19
00:01:05.259 --> 00:01:08.650
attribute design reproduces
intent, not structure.

20
00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:11.948
For each OU, record placement
and size; its GPO links,

21
00:01:11.948 --> 00:01:17.051
preferably through Get-GP-Inheritance,
which returns link order, enforcement,

22
00:01:17.051 --> 00:01:22.469
enabled state and inheritance blocking;
its non-inherited access control entries,

23
00:01:22.469 --> 00:01:27.730
with built-in principals dropped, which
are the delegations someone made by hand

24
00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:32.912
and become the administrative unit
candidates; and a text rendering for review.

25
00:01:32.912 --> 00:01:37.762
Third, Group Policy, the largest
and most consequential artifact.

26
00:01:37.762 --> 00:01:42.363
Every live setting moves to Intune,
moves elsewhere, or retires.

27
00:01:42.363 --> 00:01:44.837
Sort GPOs into three groups.

28
00:01:44.837 --> 00:01:48.013
Unlinked or empty ones
are retirement candidates.

29
00:01:48.013 --> 00:01:50.919
Overlapping settings
must be resolved first,

30
00:01:50.919 --> 00:01:54.513
because Intune's migration
refuses conflicting values.

31
00:01:54.513 --> 00:01:56.288
Live settings need a decision.

32
00:01:56.288 --> 00:02:00.845
One correction: the source searched
only OUs and the domain root,

33
00:02:00.845 --> 00:02:03.425
so site-linked GPOs looked unlinked.

34
00:02:03.425 --> 00:02:07.394
And Intune's Group Policy
analytics imports XML reports

35
00:02:07.394 --> 00:02:11.090
under four megabytes, so
check sizes in the manifest.
